>>> Nope.  Cubes are NOLIMBS, not NOHANDS.  (Convenient!)
>> Doesn't it worry anyone that NOLIMBS surly implies NOHANDS?
> 
> Does it _worry_ me?  Not really; most of the other NOLIMBS monsters are
> also flagged NOTAKE, and thus are covered that way.
> 
> The blobs and oozes aren't, and that makes sense (engulfage as pickup).  
> 
> The exploding spheres aren't, and while that doesn't make sense, it also
> doesn't worry me (never seen any of 'em pick stuff up, so it's likely
> covered somewhere anyway).  
> 
> The mimics aren't, but they're effectively NOMOVE in practice, and thus 
> NOTAKE by extension.
> 
> The lurkers, trappers, purple worms, and vortices aren't, but we're back 
> to engulfment (or GLOMPing) again, so not a big deal.

Yes, but if you name something NOHANDS then you expect it to mean that a 
monster has no hands. There are monsters which you and I consider to 
have no hands but which the nethack source treats otherwise.

What if later on I try to make a patch which means that the player can 
only cast "finger of death" when he is in a form which has hands? I 
can't use NOHANDS to achieve this goal, because a gelatinous cube player 
could still cast FoD.

Of course, there could be some clever reason the NetHack source is 
structured this way, but it just seems kinda arbitrary to me.

